  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Back in the kitchen, Leva tries to assert his new authority as the temporary head chef. He orders the cooks to work faster. Senya and Fedya support him and joke about switching to Terminator mode. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ребята, давайте работать быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У нас ещё три блюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Сейчас мы всё сделаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ну, чего вы стоите?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Шеф сказал работать быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Молодец, Лёва.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ты хороший шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ну что, мы включаем режим терминатора?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, включаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тогда быстрее за работу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Терминатор готов готовить еду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отлично, давайте быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Всё будет готово вовремя.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ребята, давайте работать быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Guys, let's work faster.' Lyova puts 'the boys' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'let's'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У нас ещё три блюда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We still have three dishes.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'us' straight to 'of dish'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Сейчас мы всё сделаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We will do everything now.' Here 'now' sets up the idea, while 'we'll do' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ну, чего вы стоите?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, why are you standing?' Senya starts with 'what?' and pairs it with 'you' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Шеф сказал работать быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The chef said to work faster.' — Notice the proper name meaning 'chef, boss' paired with the verb for 'said'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Молодец, Лёва.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well done, Leva.' Senya starts with 'well done' and pairs it with 'Lyova' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ты хороший шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are a good chef.' Senya uses the casual singular 'you' with 'you', as close colleagues and friends do. And Lyova jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, well done.' In Russian, 'well done' leads into 'well done' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ну что, мы включаем режим терминатора?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, are we switching on Terminator mode?' The first content word means 'what', and 'Terminator' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, включаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, we are switching it on.' Lyova starts with 'we're switching on' and pairs it with 'we're switching on' to make the point clear. Senya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тогда быстрее за работу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Then faster to work.' Listen for the word meaning 'back then' right alongside 'faster' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Терминатор готов готовить еду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The terminator is ready to cook food.' The key word here means 'Terminator', which Fedya combines with 'ready'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отлично, давайте быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excellent, let's go faster.' Here 'perfect' sets up the idea, while 'faster' comes at the end for emphasis. Then Senya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Всё будет готово вовремя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything will be ready on time.' You'll hear 'will be' all the time in the show, here connected with 'at the right time'. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ребята, давайте работать быстрее.",
      "gap": 0.5
